# Urban-Offline Cline Rules
# Offline-First Emergency Preparedness App
# Vision: Locally AI × Kiwix Hybrid for iOS & Android

## 1. AI Model Marketplace Management

When working with AI models:
- Use `AIModelManager.js` as the SINGLE source of truth for all model operations
- Follow the tier system strictly: essential → standard → advanced → pro
- Support both pre-configured models AND custom ONNX imports via `ModelImporter.js`
- Implement progressive download with resume capability using background fetch patterns
- Always validate model checksums before activation (SHA-256 verification)
- Cache model metadata separately from weights for instant marketplace browsing
- Store downloaded models in platform-appropriate storage with quota checks

## 2. Offline-First Architecture

When building any feature:
- Assume NO network connectivity - everything must work offline
- All critical content must function without AI models loaded (fallback templates)
- Implement graceful degradation at every architectural layer
- Use `SuspenseWrapper` for progressive UI loading with skeleton states
- Test in airplane mode before marking any feature complete
- Handle `QuotaExceededError` with user-friendly recovery options
- Ensure triage flows use Ink.js (NOT AI) for life-safety reliability

## 3. iOS/Android Feature Parity

When implementing native features:
- Use Capacitor plugins that support BOTH platforms equally
- Storage: Use `Directory.Documents` for both iOS & Android (consistent via `platform.js`)
- AI: Full Transformers.js support on both platforms (WebGL/WebGPU with fallback)
- Haptics: Use `HapticsService.js` for consistent tactile feedback across platforms
- NEVER implement platform-only features without providing equivalent functionality on the other
- Test on physical devices for both platforms before completion
- Use `isNativeMobile()`, `isIOSNative()`, `isAndroidNative()` from `platform.js` for detection

## 4. Content Pack (ZIM/Kiwix) Integration

When handling offline content packs:
- Treat ZIM files as immutable, versioned content packs (Kiwix-style)
- Validate SHA-256 checksums before importing any content
- Generate embeddings for RAG during installation, not at runtime
- Maintain `content-manifest.json` with semantic versioning
- Support delta updates for efficient content updates (only changed chunks)
- Use `DatasetRegistry.js` for enabling/disabling content packs
- Ensure content works even when AI models are unavailable

## 5. Emergency UX Standards

When designing UI flows:
- Critical content must load in <100ms (use aggressive code splitting)
- Triage flows ALWAYS use Ink.js decision trees (never AI for life-safety)
- AI responses must stream progressively with real-time citations
- Error states must provide actionable next steps (never dead ends)
- Battery-aware: Disable AI inference when battery <20% (via `BatteryManager`)
- Use `ErrorBoundary` components at page level for graceful degradation
- Implement `CriticalContentBanner` for missing essential content warnings

## 6. Code Quality Standards

When writing code:
- Use functional React components with hooks (no class components except ErrorBoundary)
- Async/await ONLY - no callback-based patterns
- ALWAYS use structured logging via `createLogger()` from `logger.js`
- Platform detection via `platform.js` utilities, never raw navigator checks
- Storage operations through `db.js` abstraction layer only
- AI operations through `AIModelManager.js` only
- Import order: React → External libs → Internal services → Components → Styles

## 7. Performance & Bundle Optimization

When adding dependencies or features:
- Lazy load all AI modules (`ai-module` chunk in vite.config.js)
- Lazy load map functionality (`map-module` chunk)
- Keep initial bundle <200KB (check `size-budget.json`)
- Use `React.lazy()` and `SuspenseWrapper` for route-level code splitting
- Monitor bundle size with `scripts/analyze-bundle-size.js`
- Prefer native Capacitor plugins over heavy JS libraries

## 8. Testing Requirements

Before marking complete:
- Test on iOS device/simulator with offline mode
- Test on Android device/emulator with offline mode
- Verify AI model download resume after network interruption
- Verify content pack install/uninstall flows
- Test with low storage (quota exceeded scenarios)
- Test with low battery (AI disable behavior)
- Run `npm run lint` with zero errors